#3007
The Common Room~
   Filled with the sounds of drinking and laughter, this is evidently a very
popular place, as nearly every table is taken.  Waitresses bustle to and fro,
making their way from the mahogany bar at the north wall to various tables.  
A fireplace in the western wallblazes orange and red, warming the room.  
Performing on a small dalies to the south, a wizened, old bard strums
beautiful tunes on his wooden harp.  The exit from the common room is to the
west, but the allure of the bar permits few to leave.
~
