#3014
The Marketplace~
   The marketplace air rings with the sharp cries of vendors hawking baked
goods, textiles, and trinkets.  The dusty roadways surrounding the grand city
square lies criss-crossed with shallow ruts made by passing carts, while
brightly colored cobbles adorn the central plaza.  The level of activity here
is overwhelming, where city guards mill about, ever ready to thwart any
potential disturbance.  High street extends east to west, while the Temple
Plaza lies to the north.  Southern Road runs off toward Meeting Square.
~
