#3024
West Ash Street~
   The stench in this area clogs the senses.  Beggars, drunks, and thieves
converge upon the ramshackle building to the south.  The cracked windows are
covered in tarpaper, and the wood looks like it's rotting.  A lopsided sign
hangs from a single chain, reading "Death's Dagger" atop a crude depiction of
a knife piercing a disembodied heart.  An odd structure to the north looks out
of place in this part of the city.  It's built to resemble the cultures of the
far east.  East of here rises the relative safety of crowded Meeting Square.
~
