#3025
The Meeting Square~
   Meeting Square, the most southerly of Heliopolis' plazas, connects to the
city's Marketplace via Southern Road, to the north.  Throngs of people mill
about, coming here to escape the Marketplace crowds, and hopefully, to avoid
the prying eyes of local authorities.  Ash Street extends both east and west,
its narrow alleyways affording minimal shelter to the homeless.  The smell of
refuse hangs in the air wafting in from the nearby town dump.  Southern Road
extends southward past the dumpsite, rising over the river into a residential
district where many of the most prominent citizens dwell.
~
