#3078
The King's Road Before the Drawbridge~
   The wide thoroughfare of King's Road ends here at the guardpost before the
castle drawbridge.  A deep, narrow moat surrounds the two sides of the castle
not abutting the city wall.  A wooden drawbridge, which is perpetually down
during these times of peace, joins the castle to the roadway.  Traffic is
congested here, as the drawbridge is not as wide as the street.
