#3079
Entrance to the Cathedral~
   The vaulted ceiling of the great cathedral rises out of sight, reaching
toward heaven it would appear.  Elaborate, stained-glass windows line the
walls, admitting filtered light, where heavy, wooden pews line the aisles.  
People fill the pews, heads bowed, praying in soft tones to their god.  
Directly before the main aisle, a great altar adorned in beautiful paintings
proclaims the greatness of your god.
