#3080
The Altar~
   At the center of the room rises a magnificent altar.  The murmur of soft
prayers and gentle chants fills the room, the high, domed ceiling reaching for
the heavens.  Numerous candles burn in a small alcove to the side of the
altar.  An enormous pipe organ fills an entire wall of the cathedral, its
tall, brass pipes reaching upward.  The exit, as well as the burdens and evils
of the world, lie to the south.
