The Monk Training Hall~
   This building has been refurbished by its present occupants to reflect
eastern decor.  Bamboo walls, rice paper doors, and hanging scrollwork serve
to set the mood.  Numerous monks practice their art in the center of the
floor.  While most are engaged in fighting, some of the aspirants practice
other talents, such as feigning death or falling from great heights.  West Ash
Street lies to the south.
